summary:
Nothing needs fixing. Since a3d3860 the only change outside the .taad slice records is docs/design/SL-020-scanner.md (e990514), and `git diff --name-only a3d3860 HEAD -- src tests eng` is empty.

The amended lines 17-19 now say:
- ChargedSize/ChargedOnDisk return 0 for a Link, for a HardlinkDuplicate entry and, since SL-042, for every Folder whatever size it states;
- they return Size/OnDisk for a File that is charged, with a pointer to docs/design/SL-042-folder-totals.md.

That matches ScanStore.Charges, which is true only for a File that is not a duplicate, and the ChargedSize/ChargedOnDisk XML docs in ScanStore.cs. It uses the fix text word for word, so O-025 is discharged.

I read the rest of SL-020-scanner.md for anything else SL-042 made false; these still hold:
- line 12: the FileId table is the only structure that rehashes;
- line 36: the probe on a FileId's first repeat, which the Scanner now triggers from the firstHolder that Append returns;
- lines 99-100: the probe opens the repeat name's own path;
- lines 114-116: an aborted first-repeat probe leaves the charged record unchanged;
- lines 20-22: charged values summed equal the Totals.

The one dated leftover is the 5M memory figure on lines 15-16 (555.9/569.9 MiB), which predates the rollup columns. It is in drift.

A grep of the repo, excluding the slice records, finds no other stale statement of the old rules: no 'every other entry', no stored child order, no folder's own size in totals, and no TryAddFileId outside the store.

On the current tree:
- incremental Release build: 0 errors;
- full Core.Tests: 199 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped;
- Fitness after rebuild: all 32 rules hold.

The code under review is byte-identical to a3d3860, which I reviewed in the previous pass, including the forced rebuild and the trx check of the timing, budget and LargestFiles tests.

